A||N||10||ssalyers||Subwoofer Install Question!!!!||||5||
Z||000000||ssalyers||10-13-2001||08:03 AM||||I just received my subwoofer that I bought from Ebay.  Can someone please tell me what needs to be removed to route the wires up to the overhead console?  Also the speaker was blown (like all of them), so I ordered one from Rodney, should I install the system and then put the subwoofer in when I get it, or just wait?<P>--Shawn||||reg||5
Z||000001||WampusCat||10-13-2001||08:53 AM||||Sorry, no clue on part one, but the actual subwoofer speaker box is easy to remove and install so taking it out later to replace the speaker is no big deal.  I just did the Rodney Dickman speaker replacement a couple of days ago.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||10-13-2001||09:07 AM||||You need to remove the door trim, sunvisors, and lower the front part of the headliner. The wires route down the passenger side A pillar. (Windshield).||||reg||1
Z||000003||ffindley||10-13-2001||09:57 AM||||Hi.  This is my first post!<P>I have Fiero Owners Club of New England's FIERO Newsletter Vol 1 Number 2 1996.  The main article is "How To Install A Fiero Sub-System".  It has 5 nicely illustrated pages for installing a stock subwoofer.  It shows very well the routing to the Overhead console.  It also includes all the parts (with GM #'s) and tools needed to complete the installation.<P>Would be happy to send you a copy of the article.  Just drop me an email.  ffindley_1@msn.com<P>------------------<BR>-----------------<BR>1988 Yellow Formula Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000004||summerjim||10-13-2001||01:36 PM||||Subwoofer install instructions here: <A HREF="http://fiero.net/txt/subinstallation.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero.net/txt/subinstallation.txt</A> <P>Walks you though everything you need to install a factory sub-system.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ssalyers||10-13-2001||02:59 PM||||Well, I did it!!!!  I fixed my door locks too (they were sticking).  But it took twice as long due to a post to this thread that said the wires went down the passenger side A-pillar.  Well, they don't!!!  But I got it done and it looks great.  It doesn't sound too great until I get my new speaker!<P>Thanks for all the help!!!<P>-Shawn||||reg||14
Z||000006||jelly2m8||10-13-2001||07:39 PM||||Heres another question on the sub install.<P>Is there a bracket for the enclosure left mounting tab for a non- AC equipped car? Or was the sub woofer option only originally available with AC equipped cars.<P>The P-22 doesn't show a bracket for non-AC cars. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||ssalyers||10-13-2001||08:10 PM||||It mount to the horn/buzzer relay box.  And the other next to the light by the door.<P>--Shawn||||reg||3
Z||000008||jelly2m8||10-14-2001||05:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ssalyers:<BR><B>It mount to the horn/buzzer relay box.  And the other next to the light by the door.<P>--Shawn</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>On a non-AC equipped Fiero, the sub enclosure left side bracket is a good 5- 6 inchs away from the relay box.<P> Obviously you didnt read my post correctly, your car must have AC.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||10-14-2001||11:43 PM||||So was it worth the work?  I have all the parts to do this install but have never taken the time to do it.  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> <BR>"And this one time, on the Fiero Forum..."||||reg||1
Z||000010||jelly2m8||10-14-2001||11:57 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DJRice:<BR><B>So was it worth the work?  I have all the parts to do this install but have never taken the time to do it.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>To me it was, the subwoofer fills the sound in nicely, giving it a nice rich sound. <P> I used Rodneys replacement speaker, which sounds great.<P> Shouldnt take more than a few hours to install everything.||||reg||1
